---
kind: scene
id: lock
on: start
once: false
title: The vault lock
state:
  scene.knocks: { type: int, default: 0 }
---
/*
Bounded backward jumps (0.51), and a declared raise.

  - The retry loop: `::tryLock` is a blocking bridge call that writes
    `scene.lock.vault.won`. The jump is taken while the lock stays shut and
    takes remain, so the loop asks at most three times (once, then two
    retries). After the second take the jump is not taken and control falls
    through to the next line.
  - The nested loop: `knock` (inner, max 2) sits inside `round` (outer,
    max 1). The inner counter returns to 0 each time control reaches `knock`
    from outside it, so each of the two rounds knocks three times:
    `scene.knocks` ends at 6.
  - `::playScene` raises `cutscene` for `scene.chapter2` once this
    presentation ends. The host does the raising; Lute draws the
    [raises] edge lock -> chapter2.
*/

## The vault door {#door}

::label{name="attempt"}
::tryLock{door="vault"}
<match subject="scene.lock.vault.won">
  <when is="false">
    @mira: Again!
    ::jump{to="attempt" max="2"}
  </when>
  <when is="true">
    @mira: It clicks open.
  </when>
</match>
@theo: That's enough for today.

## Knocking {#knocking}

::label{name="round"}
@theo: A new round.
::label{name="knock"}
::set{scene.knocks += 1}
@theo: Knock.
::jump{to="knock" max="2"}
@theo: Round done.
::jump{to="round" max="1"}

## The cutscene {#cutscene}

@theo: Now the real story.
::playScene{scene="chapter2"}
